There are two types of signal analysis:

Small-signal analysis
Large-signal analysis

These techniques are used to analyze nonlinear devices such as BJTs and diodes by replacing them with linear equivalents under suitable conditions. In small-signal analysis, the input signal is assumed to be very small compared to the DC bias level. The small AC signal is superimposed on the biasing DC voltage, and the transistor is analyzed around the Q-point. This allows us to study only a small portion of the exponential curve, which appears approximately linear.

